✨ About The Project

This project performs sentiment analysis on IMDb movie reviews using a complete NLP pipeline and a PyTorch Recurrent Neural Network (RNN).

The model classifies movie reviews into:

🟢 Positive

🔴 Negative

The project combines text preprocessing, TF-IDF feature extraction, and an RNN-based deep learning model.

🧠 Project Pipeline

flowchart LR
    A["🎬 IMDb Reviews"] --> B["🧹 Text Cleaning"]
    B --> C["✂️ Stopword Removal"]
    C --> D["🌱 Stemming"]
    D --> E["🔢 TF-IDF"]
    E --> F["🧠 PyTorch RNN"]
    F --> G["📊 Sentiment Prediction"]
    G --> H["🟢 Positive / 🔴 Negative"]

📊 Dataset

The IMDb dataset initially contains 50,000 reviews.

After removing duplicate reviews:

49,582 reviews remained.

Dataset Split

pie title Dataset Distribution
    "Training Data — 39,665" : 39665
    "Testing Data — 9,917" : 9917

Dataset

Samples

Original

50,000

After removing duplicates

49,582

Training

39,665

Testing

9,917

🔧 NLP Preprocessing

The reviews are processed through several NLP steps:

Raw Review
    ↓
Lowercase
    ↓
Remove URLs
    ↓
Remove HTML
    ↓
Remove Punctuation
    ↓
Remove Stopwords
    ↓
Porter Stemming
    ↓
Clean Text

Feature Extraction

TF-IDF is used to convert cleaned reviews into numerical features.

TfidfVectorizer(max_features=5000)

📌 5,000 features are used for model training.

🧠 RNN Architecture

The project uses a PyTorch RNN with:

Component

Configuration

Framework

PyTorch

Model

RNN

Hidden Size

128

Output

Binary sentiment

Loss

BCELoss

Optimizer

Adam

Epochs

10

Model Flow

flowchart TD
    A["TF-IDF Features<br/>5,000"] --> B["RNN"]
    B --> C["Hidden State<br/>128"]
    C --> D["Linear Layer"]
    D --> E["Binary Output"]
    E --> F["Positive / Negative"]

📈 Model Performance

The trained model achieved:

85.16% Accuracy 🎯

