🚀 How To Run

1️⃣ Clone the repository

git clone https://github.com/sumitjhadev/RNN-for-Sentiment-Analysis.git

2️⃣ Install dependencies

pip install pandas nltk scikit-learn torch

3️⃣ Open the notebook

jupyter notebook

Then open:

imdb-sentiment-analysis-rnn.ipynb

4️⃣ Run all cells

The notebook will:

Load Dataset
     ↓
Preprocess Reviews
     ↓
Create TF-IDF Features
     ↓
Train RNN
     ↓
Evaluate Model
     ↓
Display Accuracy

🎯 Key Highlights

📝 IMDb movie review classification

🧹 Complete NLP preprocessing pipeline

🔤 Stopword removal & stemming

📊 TF-IDF feature extraction

🧠 PyTorch RNN implementation

⚡ Adam optimization

🎯 85.16% test accuracy

📌 Result

The project demonstrates how traditional NLP preprocessing + TF-IDF features + a Recurrent Neural Network can be combined to classify movie reviews into positive and negative sentiments.

